22-01
00:26:49.364 --> 00:26:53.588
This is the pressure-case result in the actual calculator.

22-02
00:26:53.768 --> 00:27:04.408
At three hundred and fifty kelvin and four hundred kilopascals, the
selected route still gives K equal to about three point nine five
three two six.

22-03
00:27:04.588 --> 00:27:11.436
The extent is about zero point four four five one one moles,
consistent with case twelve B.

22-04
00:27:11.616 --> 00:27:18.251
The species table lets you reconstruct both the atom balance and the
equilibrium quotient.

22-05
00:27:18.431 --> 00:27:22.634
Now inspect the Gibbs-energy curve along reaction extent.

22-06
00:27:22.814 --> 00:27:31.219
Its minimum occurs at the calculated equilibrium extent for this
fixed-temperature, fixed-pressure ideal gas model.

22-07
00:27:31.399 --> 00:27:38.596
The vertical axis is the change in total Gibbs energy from the
reference state, divided by R T.

22-08
00:27:38.776 --> 00:27:40.568
Its units are moles.

22-09
00:27:40.748 --> 00:27:48.705
This plotted quantity is different from standard reaction Gibbs energy
and from the actual reaction Gibbs energy.

22-10
00:27:48.885 --> 00:27:55.861
The actual reaction Gibbs energy is the slope of total Gibbs energy
with respect to extent.

22-11
00:27:56.041 --> 00:28:00.862
The minimum tells us where the slope with respect to extent becomes
zero.

22-12
00:28:01.042 --> 00:28:05.501
The allowed interval still comes from nonnegative species amounts.

22-13
00:28:05.681 --> 00:28:11.014
Lab twelve solves one balanced reaction among neutral ideal gases.

22-14
00:28:11.194 --> 00:28:20.368
It does not automatically calculate liquid splitting, multiple
simultaneous reactions or a nonideal equation of state.

22-15
00:28:20.548 --> 00:28:27.716
These limits belong beside the numerical answer when you describe what
the calculation establishes.

23-01
00:28:30.246 --> 00:28:33.147
