31-01
00:38:49.064 --> 00:38:54.141
Before the final form, check the explanation you would give to another
student.

31-02
00:38:54.321 --> 00:38:59.804
K follows from standard thermodynamic properties and the chosen
temperature.

31-03
00:38:59.984 --> 00:39:03.824
Q follows from the activities of a particular state.

31-04
00:39:04.004 --> 00:39:11.343
Equilibrium extent combines the equilibrium condition with the feed
and conservation constraints.

31-05
00:39:11.523 --> 00:39:16.041
These three ideas work together, but they answer different questions.

31-06
00:39:16.221 --> 00:39:20.125
The inert-gas question also depends on the constraint.

31-07
00:39:20.305 --> 00:39:29.095
In this Lab, adding inert at fixed temperature and total pressure
dilutes the reacting species and can shift the equilibrium.

31-08
00:39:29.275 --> 00:39:43.183
In a rigid ideal gas vessel at fixed temperature and volume, adding
inert leaves reacting-species partial pressures unchanged, so an
initially equilibrated reacting mixture does not shift.

31-09
00:39:43.363 --> 00:39:47.075
Name the constraint whenever you use that conclusion.

31-10
